{% comment %}
  "Meet Walter" — the person behind Walterin.

  Typography is INTENTIONALLY identical to the "About Walterin" rich-text section:
  - Heading uses a real <h2 class="h1"> so it inherits Dawn's heading rules exactly
    (WalterinBold, .h1 size 3.25rem mobile / 4.225rem desktop, theme line-height
    + letter-spacing) — same element/class About Walterin uses.
  - Body mirrors the theme body exactly: 1.5rem, line-height calc(1 + 0.8/scale),
    letter-spacing 0.06rem, var(--font-body-family) (Inter), colour #2e2a39.
  The ONLY deliberate difference from About Walterin is alignment: this section is
  LEFT-aligned (About is centred). Background stays cream to read distinct from the
  white About section directly above it.

  Photo defaults to assets/wi-walter.jpg. Owns the .mw-* namespace only.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  if section.settings.photo_image != blank
    assign photo_src = section.settings.photo_image | image_url: width: 700
    assign photo_w = 700
    assign photo_h = 973
  else
    assign photo_asset = section.settings.photo_asset | default: 'wi-walter.jpg'
    assign photo_src = photo_asset | asset_url
    assign photo_w = 1100
    assign photo_h = 1530
  endif
-%}

{%- style -%}
  .mw-section {
    background: {{ section.settings.background | default: '#FFFEF7' }};
    padding: 52px 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid #ece9e1; /* subtle separation from the section above */
  }
  .mw-inner {
    max-width: 1240px;            /* same content boundary as the other sections */
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 1fr);  /* small photo + wide text */
    gap: clamp(36px, 5vw, 72px);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .mw-photo {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 220px;
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 56px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
  }
  .mw-photo img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border-radius: inherit; }

  .mw-text { text-align: left; }
  /* Heading: only colour + spacing here — size/font/line-height/letter-spacing all
     come from Dawn's .h1 + heading rules, so it is identical to About Walterin. */
  .mw-heading {
    color: #2e2a39;
    margin: 0 0 1.8rem;
  }
  /* Body: identical to About Walterin / the theme body. */
  .mw-body p {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: calc(1 + 0.8 / var(--font-body-scale, 1));
    letter-spacing: 0.06rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body-family);
    color: #2e2a39;
    margin: 0 0 1.8rem;
  }
  .mw-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .mw-body strong { font-weight: var(--font-body-weight-bold, 700); }
  .mw-body em { font-style: italic; }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .mw-section { padding: 40px 22px; }
    .mw-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 22px;
      justify-items: start;
    }
    .mw-photo { max-width: 170px; }
  }
{%- endstyle -%}

<section class="mw-section">
  <div class="mw-inner">
    <figure class="mw-photo">
      <img
        src="{{ photo_src }}"
        alt="{{ section.settings.photo_alt | default: 'Walter Ihring, the illustrator behind Walterin' | escape }}"
        width="{{ photo_w }}"
        height="{{ photo_h }}"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      >
    </figure>
    <div class="mw-text">
      <h2 class="mw-heading h1">{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Hi. My name is Walter Ihring.' | escape }}</h2>
      <div class="mw-body">
        <p>{{ section.settings.paragraph_1 }}</p>
        <p>{{ section.settings.paragraph_2 }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Meet Walter",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-meet-walter",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Hi. My name is Walter Ihring."
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "paragraph_1",
      "label": "Paragraph 1",
      "default": "I devote my time to <strong>animated humour and caricatures</strong>. I like travelling, especially across India. My pictures also like travelling, especially for exhibitions in cities far away. On their return, they sometimes bring me an award as a souvenir from the competitions they had visited."
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "paragraph_2",
      "label": "Paragraph 2",
      "default": "On one hot day in summer, I was sipping my coffee in the square, watching tourists race from the town hall to the cathedral, hunting for the stories of the people who lived there. It was there that I decided to link sketching with history, travelling and humour — and create amusing illustrated guides. In 2015 I published my first, about my hometown, <strong>Walterin Bratislava</strong>."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Photo"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "photo_asset",
      "label": "Photo asset filename (in assets/)",
      "info": "Used when no custom image is chosen. e.g. wi-walter.jpg",
      "default": "wi-walter.jpg"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "photo_image",
      "label": "Custom photo (overrides the asset above)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "photo_alt",
      "label": "Photo alt text",
      "default": "Walter Ihring, the illustrator behind Walterin"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "Background",
      "default": "#FFFEF7"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Meet Walter" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
